-- title:
--   Theorem 3.3, p. 180 — under Assumption 3.1, a non-terminating run of Algorithm 2.1 has liminf ‖g_k‖ = 0
-- statement:
--   Let $f:\mathbb R^n\to\mathbb R$ and let $0<\delta<\sigma<1$. Suppose that $x_1$ is a starting point for which Assumption 3.1 holds: $f$ is bounded below on $\mathbb R^n$ and continuously differentiable in an open neighbourhood $\mathcal N$ of the level set $\mathcal L=\{x: f(x)\le f(x_1)\}$, and $\|\nabla f(x)-\nabla f(y)\|\le L\|x-y\|$ for all $x,y\in\mathcal N$, with $L>0$.
--
--   Let $\{x_k\}_{k\ge1}$ be generated by Algorithm 2.1 (the Dai–Yuan conjugate gradient method): $d_1=-g_1$, $x_{k+1}=x_k+\alpha_kd_k$ with $\alpha_k>0$ satisfying the standard Wolfe conditions
--   $$f(x_k)-f(x_k+\alpha_kd_k)\ge-\delta\alpha_kg_k^Td_k,\qquad g(x_k+\alpha_kd_k)^Td_k>\sigma g_k^Td_k,$$
--   and $d_{k+1}=-g_{k+1}+\beta_kd_k$ with $\beta_k=\|g_{k+1}\|^2/d_k^Ty_k$, $y_k=g_{k+1}-g_k$. If the algorithm does not terminate, i.e. $g_k\neq0$ for every $k\ge1$, then
--   $$\liminf_{k\to\infty}\|g_k\|=0 .$$
--
--   This is the main result of the paper: unlike the Fletcher–Reeves, Polak–Ribière–Polyak and Hestenes–Stiefel methods, the Dai–Yuan method converges under the *standard* (not strong) Wolfe line search, and without assuming a bounded level set.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Algorithm 2.1 stops (at Step 1 or Step 3) exactly when $g_k=0$, i.e. at a stationary point; that is the first alternative of the paper's theorem ("terminates at a stationary point"). The formal statement is the other alternative: the run is infinite, encoded as $g_k\neq0$ for all $k\ge1$ (the paper's (3.8)). $\liminf\|g_k\|=0$ is stated as: for every $\varepsilon>0$ and every $K$ there is $k\ge K$ with $\|g_k\|<\varepsilon$. "Continuously differentiable in $\mathcal N$" is differentiability at every point of the open set $\mathcal N$ with $\nabla f$ continuous on $\mathcal N$. The curvature condition is strict, as printed. $\beta_k$ is a Lean division; along a run its denominator is positive. No descent property, no positivity of $d_k^Ty_k$ and no Zoutendijk condition is assumed: these are the milestones.
-- source:
--   Dai and Yuan, A nonlinear conjugate gradient method with a strong global convergence property, SIAM J. Optim. 10 (1999), p. 180, Theorem 3.3 and (3.7)

